position.description:
Development of a generic platform-independent power management function for safety-critical systems for autonomous driving vehicles.
1. This master thesis describes the development of a generic power management platform for safety-critical systems for autonomous driving vehicles;
2. This power management shall provide safe startup, shutdown, and mode change between different processors within a multi-domain controller for all applications and controls power consumption inside the module;
3. The function includes standby, sleep, or power-saving modes in order to reduce power consumption to a necessary minimum;
4. 	The design includes:
          a)  System Context and System Function design;
          b) Functionality for the involved system elements;
          c) The interfaces between system elements and functions;
          d) State machine for the designed functions;
          e) Implementation in Matlab, Stateflow, and Simulink.

